PrefaceClimate change is one of the greatest challenges to humanity’s future and worsening of extreme weather is at the leading edge of concerns. The most extreme weather events contribute disproportionately to risk amplification because they account for such a large share of total impacts, and can trigger cascading consequences. Yet our ability to pre-empt such events is limited. In this Perspective, we urge more targeted research combining the power of human imagination with improved understanding of what is possible across impact-relevant systems—including in extreme climate states—to help identify, and avoid, catastrophic consequences from climate change.

